Fix asset + preview-link paths for project-page deploys
The CI workflow now reads actions/configure-pages's `base_path` output
and passes it as `--baseurl` to every Jekyll build. This makes the same
codebase work whether the repo deploys as a USER page (foo.github.io,
base_path is "") or as a PROJECT page (foo.github.io/repo, base_path
is "/repo"). The five build invocations are:

  Live:     --baseurl "$BASE_PATH"
  Preview:  --baseurl "$BASE_PATH/_preview/<theme>"

The preview-switcher computes the deploy root from site.baseurl by
stripping any "/_preview/<theme>" suffix, so cross-preview links and
the "back to my site" link resolve correctly under either deploy.

